    "ask": [
      "mcp__pipeboard__create_campaign",
      "mcp__pipeboard__create_adset",
      "mcp__pipeboard__create_ad_rule",
      "mcp__pipeboard__upload_ad_video"
    ]
  },
  "_comment": "The write guard for the ads part. deny: 60 Pipeboard tools an unattended run never needs (targeting and ad-set edits, deletes, duplicates, audiences, rules, catalogs, posts, account slots) plus Meta's own connector (mcp__meta-ads), which the prompts never use. ask: the build-time writes (new campaign, new ad set, new Meta rule, a video from a URL) stop for a human even in Auto mode, so they only happen while the operator watches. The check-in keeps update_ad, update_campaign, create_ad_creative, create_existing_post_ad_creative, create_ad, create_video_upload_url, upload_ad_video_file, upload_ad_image and the read tools. Keyed to a server named pipeboard, as ads/SETUP.md adds it; under another name the check-in reports and changes nothing."
}
